ectronically Signed Out By  Atul K Bhan MBBS  MD on REMOVED_DATE 12 41       CLINICAL HISTORY  65 year old female with left breast calcifications  lower inner quadrant     DCIS  Calcifications are in the cassette     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST CORE BIOPSY  LEFT LOWER INNER QUADRANT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Aliberti    REMOVED_CASE_ID  and  left  breast   is an aggregate of fibroadipose tissue admixed with hemorrhagic tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the  same container  removed from an orange cassette  is an aggregate of fibroadipose  tissue admixed with hemorrhagic tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  submitted  in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Immunohistochemical and in situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts  General Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics  determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of  Pathology at Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or  approved by the U S Food and Drug Administration  FDA   the FDA has determined  that such clearance or approval is not necessary       PART   BREAST CORE BIOPSY  LEFT LOWER INNER QUADRANT       report_end  , Unknown.
