om the anterior margin  There is focal hemorrhage and cyst formation medial to the mass  The remaining parenchyma is yellow  lobulated  and unremarkable  The axillary region is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly identified  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic area medial to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic area lateral to mass  Received fresh  labeled  right mastectomy flap   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm strip of tan  unremarkable skin  excised to the depth of 0 2cm  The specimen is inked black and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The low grade tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The low grade tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The low grade tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  The high grade tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The high grade tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Focally  the high grade tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visual