Immediately anterior to this cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm biopsy cavity with surrounding tan white fibrous tissue and yellow tan firm areas  The biopsy cavity is directly underlying the skin ellipse  just medial and superior to the nipple  No residual mass is identified  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm area of tan white fibrous tissue in the central area of the breast just lateral to the skin ellipse  There is also an area of tan white fibrous tissue in the upper outer quadrant near the axillary tail  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of yellow tan fatty tissue and occasional tan pink and fibrous tissue  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the upper outer quadrant  A photograph of the implant is taken  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative from central fibrous area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative from superior medial fibrous area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One large lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary fibrous area  Gross Dictation by Paul N Staats  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paul N Staats  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unknown.
