east carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 97 at 15 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in multiple parts  Labeled  re excision  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm skin ellipse with an underlying REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast parenchyma with a short stitch designating superior  a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is inked with the long lateral margin inked green  short or superior margin black  inferior margin black  anterior margin blue  posterior margin red  medial margin yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity 1 5cm beneath the skin ellipse  Contains surrounding ill defined firm  bright yellow and tan to yellow tissue  but without any definite nodules or masses  Areas of firm  bright yellow tissue abut the green and blue margins  anterior lateral margin   The remainder of the breast reveals areas of ill defined white to tan firm tissue  Section code  A D  biopsy cavity E H  representative sections of abnormal surrounding tissue I  long or lateral margin with abnormal tissue Labeled  additional anterior inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue inked and entirely submitted in J  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue sectioned to reveal multiple pink tan lymph nodes  the largest measuring 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections in K 0  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL